.TH DAYTONA-THEMETOOL 1 "November 2026" "Daytona 0.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
daytona-themetool \- apply Windows colour schemes and .theme files to Daytona
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B daytona-themetool inspect
\fIFILE.theme\fR | \fB\-\-scheme\fR \fINAME\fR
.br
.B daytona-themetool apply
\fIFILE.theme\fR | \fB\-\-scheme\fR \fINAME\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B inspect
prints the colours, wallpaper and cursors of a Windows 95, NT or Plus!
\&.theme file or a built-in scheme (Daytona Classic, Daytona Standard, High
Contrast Black, High Contrast White), with warnings for parts Daytona does not support.
.PP
.B apply
makes it the current scheme: it writes
\fI$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/daytona/colors.ini\fR (followed live by the shell and Qt
applications using the daytona style), a labwc window theme and a GTK 3 theme
under \fI$XDG_DATA_HOME/themes/Daytona\fR (removed again for Windows
Standard), sets the Chicago95 icon and cursor themes for GTK, and copies a
\&.theme file's wallpaper. A running labwc is told to reload its theme.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR daytona-shell (1)
